<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Münsingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1482</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Münsingen of 1482 reunited the County of Württemberg, which had been divided in 1442 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-urach">Urach</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a> lines. Agreed between Count Eberhard V the Bearded and his cousin Eberhard VI, it declared the county indivisible under the senior ruler, with Stuttgart as its capital, and prepared the way for Württemberg's elevation to a duchy in 1495.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-munsingen.jpg" alt="Treaty of Münsingen" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:900-103_M%C3%BCnsinger_Vertrag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
